00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:40.490
- Alright, learning to cook

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:43.800
Cha Cha fried coconut chicken, take one.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.430
- And how do you prepare that chicken?

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:48.430
- It goes through a one
day marinating process.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:52.393
Citrus, orange, cinnamon,
cloves, allspice, jerk spice.

00:02:53.273 --> 00:02:55.689
It's been marinated for a day,

00:02:55.689 --> 00:02:56.522
then it gets oven roasted,

00:02:56.522 --> 00:02:57.860
and then from there, gets braised

00:02:57.860 --> 00:02:59.720
in the kind of like, sauce?

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:02.210
- So it's roasted, and
then you put the breading--

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:03.163
- Exactly.
- And then you fry it.

00:03:03.163 --> 00:03:05.273
- Wow.
- And have it soaking

00:03:05.273 --> 00:03:06.240
in the literally, the coconut milk.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:07.970
So we're gonna put a
little bit of regular,

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:10.280
all-purpose flour into our chicken,

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:12.009
just to get it started there.

00:03:12.009 --> 00:03:13.133
- You're putting the flour in the chicken,

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:15.173
not the chicken into the flour.

00:03:15.173 --> 00:03:16.285
- Usually--
- No, no.

00:03:16.285 --> 00:03:17.118
- Reverse, reverse.

00:03:17.118 --> 00:03:17.951
Cha Cha real smooth.

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:20.460
